# Sovalune Model Runtime

## Overview
C++/CUDA inference engine for Sovalune AI models with llama.cpp backend.

## Features
- GGUF model loading via llama.cpp
- CUDA acceleration with cuBLAS
- CPU-only mode for development
- REST API (OpenAI-compatible)
- NATS messaging for distributed inference
- Tool calling support
- Streaming token generation

## Project Structure
```
sovalune-model-runtime/
├── src/
│   ├── engine/          # Core inference engine
│   │   ├── inference_engine.cpp/hpp  # Main engine wrapper
│   │   ├── llama_backend.cpp/hpp     # llama.cpp integration
│   │   ├── engine_config.cpp/hpp     # Configuration
│   │   └── gpu_manager.cpp/hpp       # CUDA device management
│   ├── server/          # REST API
│   │   └── rest_api_server.cpp/hpp   # OpenAI-compatible API
│   ├── tool_calling/    # Tool call parsing
│   ├── nats_bridge/     # NATS messaging
│   ├── tokenizer/       # Token counting
│   └── main.cpp         # Entry point
├── CMakeLists.txt       # Build configuration
├── build.sh             # Build script
├── Makefile             # Make targets
├── Dockerfile           # Docker image (CPU)
├── Dockerfile.cuda      # Docker image (CUDA)
└── docker-compose.yml   # Docker Compose setup
```

## Build Commands
```bash
# CPU build
make

# CUDA build
make cuda

# Debug build
make debug

# Clean
make clean
```

## Environment Variables
- `SOVALUNE_MODEL_PATH` - Path to GGUF model
- `SOVALUNE_RUNTIME_MODE` - cpu or cuda
- `SOVALUNE_NATS_URL` - NATS server URL
- `SOVALUNE_REST_PORT` - REST API port
